{"id":"e1d430cdc0e4cc29","group":"68","path":"68/68-df-effective-join.md","title":"Effective Join","display":"df-effective-join — Effective Join","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Recursion Theory (Shoenfield)","book_abbrev":"68","label":"68-df-effective-join","aliases":["68-df-effective-join"],"display":"df-effective-join — Effective Join","depends_on":["[[68-df-natural-number]]"],"source_edition":"1993 original; 2016 Cambridge reissue, supplied PDF","source_location":"§15 proposition 15.1 p.54 / PDF 63; binary set encoding variant","verification_status":"source-adapted-definition","source_proof_status":"not-checked"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Recursion Theory (Shoenfield)"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"68"},{"key":"label","html":"68-df-effective-join"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>68-df-effective-join</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-effective-join — Effective Join"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"3368c1852f2a1aa0\" href=\"?note=3368c1852f2a1aa0\" title=\"68-df-natural-number\">68-df-natural-number</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"1993 original; 2016 Cambridge reissue, supplied PDF"},{"key":"source_location","html":"§15 proposition 15.1 p.54 / PDF 63; binary set encoding variant"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-adapted-definition"},{"key":"source_proof_status","html":"not-checked"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,B\\subseteq\\mathbb N\">\\(A,B\\subseteq\\mathbb N\\)</span>，自然数见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"3368c1852f2a1aa0\" href=\"?note=3368c1852f2a1aa0\" title=\"68-df-natural-number\">68-df-natural-number</a>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"A\\oplus B:=\\{2x:x\\in A\\}\\cup\\{2x+1:x\\in B\\}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[A\\oplus B:=\\{2x:x\\in A\\}\\cup\\{2x+1:x\\in B\\}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>原书 15.1 以实数值的有限元组构造共同上界；此处用偶数位与奇数位的集合版本，两个坐标均可有效恢复。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"68-df-natural-number","status":"resolved","id":"3368c1852f2a1aa0","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[68-df-natural-number]]","embed":false},{"target":"68-df-natural-number","status":"resolved","id":"3368c1852f2a1aa0","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$A,B\\subseteq\\mathbb N$，自然数见 [[68-df-natural-number]]。","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"A,B\\subseteq\\mathbb N","display":false},{"tex":"A\\oplus B:=\\{2x:x\\in A\\}\\cup\\{2x+1:x\\in B\\}.","display":true}],"bytes":820,"backlinks":[{"id":"4ed6f28789f0aa57","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathbf a,\\mathbf b\\in\\mathcal D$，$\\deg$ 见 [[68-df-turing-degree]]，集合 $\\oplus$ 见 [[68-df-effective-join]]。以下重载 $\\oplus$ 的参数均为度。"},{"id":"e061a6cb0c6ad653","anchor":"ref-12","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$G\\subseteq\\mathbb N$，$\\mathrm{1\\text{-}Generic}$ 见 [[68-df-one-generic-set]]。$\\mathrm{Recursive}$、跳跃 $G'$、$\\equiv_T$、有效并 $\\oplus$ 分别见 [[68-df-recursive-set]]、[[68-df-turing-jump]]、[[68-df-turing-equivalence]]、[[68-df-effective-join]]。oracle 程序及其有限查询性质见 [[68-df-oracle-computation]]、[[68-thm-oracle-finite-use]]。"},{"id":"f850298d5e806601","anchor":"ref-53","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[68-df-effective-join]]"},{"id":"be41c4d7dd143cb1","anchor":"ref-22","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"